cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  OpenMP Offloading Intra-node Bandwidth Benchmarks:
  NVIDIA H100, AMD MI250X and Intel Data Center GPU Max 1550
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite both the artifact itself
  and the accompanying paper.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Krishnasamy
    given-names: Ezhilmathi
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1971-4973'
    # affiliation: '[Your institution]'
abstract: >-
  Benchmarks comparing OpenMP target offload against each vendor's native
  programming model (CUDA, HIP and SYCL) for intra-node data movement on
  NVIDIA H100, AMD MI250X and Intel Data Center GPU Max 1550 GPUs. Covers
  synchronous and asynchronous host-to-device and device-to-host transfers,
  and peer-to-peer transfers between devices. Includes the raw measurement
  data, so every figure in the paper can be regenerated without GPU access.
keywords:
  - OpenMP
  - GPU offloading
  - performance portability
  - memory bandwidth
  - CUDA
  - HIP
  - SYCL
  - NVIDIA H100
  - AMD MI250X
  - Intel Ponte Vecchio
